// Package logging builds this service's logger and owns the log schema.
//
// Belongs here: the handler that renders the two tiers (a human console form
// for local development, one JSON object per line everywhere else), the
// reserved-field block, trace correlation, and redaction.
//
// Does NOT belong here: log call sites. Those live wherever the interesting
// thing happened.
//
// The field set is defined in docs/logging.md and nowhere else. Mint's
// `make parity` boots a service in each language and diffs the emitted keys
// against that document, so a field invented at a call site is a parity
// failure rather than a nice extra.
//
// Empty until Mint chunk 04. Until then the service prints one plain startup
// line, and that is not a log record — do not build on it.
package logging
